{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "ewHVmXbmr8GN43NIj",
			"description": "Frag Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard fragmentation grenade of the Departmento Munitorum, a fist-sized charge issued to virtually every Guardsman; a background constant across Black Library Guard fiction from Gaunt's Ghosts to the Ciaphas Cain novels.\n\nDesign: No framework.md anchor covers grenades, so this is built independently using GURPS's own explosive-damage convention — a concussion \"cr ex\" figure plus a bracketed fragmentation die, exactly the pattern data-format.md's own schema example uses. Concussion is set to a modest 3d cr ex (enough to injure at the centre, nowhere near a demolition charge) with a 4d cut fragmentation cloud (user direction, down from 6d: at 6d the fragments reached 30 yards and shredded massed infantry under B414) as the real threat to exposed infantry within a few yards. 4d cut (avg 14, no armour divisor) never penetrates flak (DR 30) or carapace (DR 70); only the Weak Points roll lets a fragment through flak. It is lethal to unarmoured troops in the open and useless against armour or fortifications.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "20",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WWR_FxjOQl1NiBlcB",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr ex",
						"base": "3d",
						"fragmentation": "4d",
						"fragmentation_type": "cut"
					},
					"usage": "Thrown",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eEGPd6DfrgIA6xDzN",
			"description": "Krak Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Imperium's standard anti-armour and anti-fortification grenade, issued alongside frag grenades to Guard and Astartes forces alike; codex and Black Library background repeatedly show it wrecking light vehicles and bunker firing points, and occasionally cracking heavier targets at real cost and risk.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a hand-thrown shaped charge using the same \"cr ex plus armour divisor\" logic GURPS uses for anti-tank warheads, kept well below the meltagun anchor (8dx6(10) burn to ½D) in both multiplier and divisor: a grenade-sized shaped charge carries an order of magnitude less fuel and a much less focused liner than a dedicated melta weapon's thermal lance, so it keeps the mundane armour divisor of (2) rather than melta's (10). Required vehicle-armour check against framework.md's AV-to-DR table, by exact dice distribution (6dx4, average 84, divisor 2): AV10 (DR 125, effective 62) penetrates 90.4% of hits — \"reliable\" against the lightest vehicles. AV11 (DR 185, effective 92) drops to 27.9%, only \"sometimes,\" and AV12 (DR 250, effective 125) to a negligible 0.5% (only rolls of 32+ on 6d clear it). AV13 (DR 340, effective 170) and AV14 (DR 440, effective 220) are a flat 0% — the maximum possible roll (6d of 36, times 4 = 144) can never reach them — so a krak grenade cannot crack a Chimera's front, a Leman Russ or a Land Raider at all. This matches the lore's use of krak grenades as light-vehicle and infantry-support ordnance rather than a dedicated tank-killer — that job belongs to the meltagun and melta bomb.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "60",
			"base_weight": "1.5 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WhHpNRRx41eSmllVY",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr ex",
						"base": "6dx4",
						"armor_divisor": 2
					},
					"usage": "Thrown, shaped charge",
					"usage_notes": "Contact-fused shaped charge with a very small blast radius (roughly 1 yard) — built for a single hard target, not an area effect.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "e8kIcbTj8cSMlP-1z",
			"description": "Melta Bomb",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A hefty demolition charge with an integral melta-coil detonator, carried by sappers and Techmarines to crack void-hull bulkheads, bunkers and vehicle hulls when a meltagun isn't available or isn't enough; Black Library fiction shows melta bombs destroying Land Raiders and fortifications when a Space Marine or Guard sapper can get one physically onto the target.\n\nDesign: Uses the same superheated thermal-lance principle as the meltagun anchor (8dx6(10) burn to ½D) and keeps its armour divisor of (10) unchanged — it's the same fuel-air/thermic mechanism, just a bigger charge. The satchel-sized reservoir carries proportionally more fuel than a meltagun's cell, set roughly 1.25x above the meltagun's figure by average damage: 6dx10 averages 210, about 1.25x the meltagun's own 8dx6 average of 168. Sanity check against the toughest anchor, by exact dice distribution: AV14 (DR 440) is reduced to an effective DR 44 by the divisor, and even the minimum possible roll (6 dice all showing 1, x10 = 60) clears that — a melta bomb beats AV14 on 100% of hits, guaranteed. Against the DR 1350 glacis of a Leman Russ front or a Land Raider (effective DR 135) it still penetrates 96.4% of hits, against the meltagun's 87%. That's stronger than \"usually\" and is deliberate: a hand-placed, contact-fused charge doesn't suffer a meltagun's range falloff, so it should be the single most reliable anti-tank tool in the Imperium's arsenal, consistent with it being a dedicated, single-use, last-resort tank-killer rather than a weapon anyone carries casually (LC1, high cost).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "250",
			"base_weight": "6 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "W75fn78DfyOe5xd2k",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn",
						"base": "6dx10",
						"armor_divisor": 10
					},
					"usage": "Placed charge (contact, timed or remote-detonated)",
					"usage_notes": "Hand-placed against a hull, hatch or wall; not thrown and not usable at range. Arming and placing it well enough to guarantee the shot is a demolitions task, rolled against Explosives (Demolition).",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Explosives"
							},
							"specialization": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Demolition"
							}
						},
