		{
			"id": "eIIiAsU8jyxh5N_gZ",
			"description": "Photon Flash Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A dazzling photonic flash grenade used by the Guard and the Adeptus Arbites for room-clearing and riot control; consistently shown as a non-lethal, temporary-blindness tool rather than a casualty-producing weapon.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a GURPS Affliction-style blinding attack (per Basic Set's flash-grenade conventions) using a flat HT roll rather than a damage roll, since a photon flash grenade's entire purpose is sensory disruption rather than physical injury. No dedicated GCS damage type exists for this, so \"spec\" (special) is used and the actual mechanic is spelled out in the notes field, which is read at the table.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "25",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "W8AM7tmp9IugrhLPk",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "spec"
					},
					"usage": "Flash",
					"usage_notes": "Everyone within 5 yards facing the grenade when it goes off must roll vs. HT-6 or be blinded for 1d minutes; anyone looking away or wearing eye protection is unaffected. Deals no HP damage.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "ess8bQp2O98izzBCT",
			"description": "Blind Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Several RPG-line sourcebooks use \"blind grenade\" and \"photon flash grenade\" almost interchangeably; honestly, no single source draws a hard line between them. This entry treats the blind grenade as the cruder, more common cousin of the Guard's issued photon flash grenade — a chemical flash-charge rather than a calibrated photonic burst, and correspondingly cheaper and more widely available.\n\nDesign: Same Affliction-style blinding effect as the Photon Flash Grenade, but a shallower HT-4 roll to be blinded, reflecting the cruder, less reliable dazzle mechanism implied by its lower cost and wider availability (LC3 vs. the photon flash's more standardised issue).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "18",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WxdhfS-AYAqAtFq1K",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "spec"
					},
					"usage": "Flash",
					"usage_notes": "Everyone within 5 yards facing the grenade when it goes off must roll vs. HT-4 or be blinded for 1d minutes; anyone looking away or wearing eye protection is unaffected. Deals no HP damage.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "e-bCBKlDsy4MwI6tA",
			"description": "Smoke Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Fills a roughly 5-yard-radius area with heavy smoke starting the turn after it lands, blocking normal vision through the cloud (treat as Dark, B358) for several minutes depending on wind; auspex and thermal sights may partially see through it at the GM's discretion.\n\nLore: The standard obscurant grenade issued to virtually every Imperial infantry force for cover during an advance or a withdrawal — one of the least remarkable and most universally carried pieces of Guard wargear.\n\nDesign: No attack roll applies, so there's no `weapons` entry; the area effect is written directly into the rules-text `notes` field using GURPS's existing smoke/vision rules (B358) rather than inventing a new mechanic for it.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_value": "15",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "ehX1P97WQPspDtpY1",
			"description": "Stun Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A non-lethal concussive grenade used by the Adeptus Arbites, ship security details and Inquisitorial forces for taking suspects alive rather than killing them.\n\nDesign: Deliberately weak on raw damage (1d cr, rarely more than a bruise) because its purpose is the HT roll it forces, not the blast itself — the same additional-effect logic GURPS flashbangs use. The small crushing damage represents the physical concussion of the charge.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Arbites"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "30",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"weapons": [
