				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eOcvBZwcsZ9d3EELb",
			"description": "Plasma Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A rare, expensive superheated-plasma grenade, more commonly referenced in Horus Heresy-era and elite Inquisitorial/Deathwatch matériel than standard Guard issue; included here as the thrown cousin of the plasma gun, honestly noted as an uncommon item rather than standard-issue wargear.\n\nDesign: Scaled down from the plasma gun anchor (6dx4(3) burn ex) at half the base dice count (3d of the anchor's 6d, keeping the x4 multiplier and the (3) divisor unchanged): a hand-thrown plasma charge has an even smaller containment cell than a plasma pistol's, but it's still the same superheated-plasma penetration principle, so the divisor carries over unmodified. Average roll 42 comfortably beats carapace (DR 70, effective 23.3: 95.4% of hits) and Sororitas plate (DR 85, effective 28.3: 83.8%), and still gets through Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective 33.3) on 74.1% of hits — a rare grenade that can seriously hurt a Space Marine, matching plasma's place as the one small-arms family that reliably threatens power armour. The canonical containment-failure/overheat hazard of plasma technology is noted as flavour rather than modelled numerically, matching how the plasma gun anchor itself just references \"Malfunction\" without a schema field for it.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "500",
			"base_weight": "2 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WkbPRXKX1Vv8DVzBK",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn ex",
						"base": "3dx4",
						"armor_divisor": 3
					},
					"usage": "Thrown",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eRVmQ_ZSO--Oed4zS",
			"description": "Haywire Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An anti-vehicle, anti-servitor EMP charge used by Guard tank-hunter teams and Inquisitorial forces against constructs and unshielded machine-spirits; background material notes it as effective but unpredictable against lightly shielded war machines, and useless against anything that isn't substantially mechanical.\n\nDesign: Deals no HP damage at all — modelled purely as a systems-disable effect (the \"spec\" damage type plus rules text) rather than a damage roll, matching how GURPS treats EMP-style weapons as a disruption effect rather than a wounding one.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "150",
			"base_weight": "1.5 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "Wq_aHGZSLnTRogyFF",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "spec"
					},
					"usage": "EMP burst",
					"usage_notes": "No effect on living flesh. Vehicles, robots and servitors within 2 yards have all active systems (weapons, engines, augur/vox) disabled for 2d turns unless the GM rules the target is shielded; against a Machine Spirit-bound war engine (Dreadnoughts, Sentinels and the like), treat this as an unusually harsh HT roll instead of an automatic effect.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eO34j8A2iKkdmo5eI",
			"description": "Grenade Launcher",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A break-action or revolver-cylinder launcher used by Guard grenadiers and heavy-weapon teams to put frag or krak payloads well past throwing range; a mainstay support weapon across Astra Militarum background art and fiction.\n\nDesign: The damage lines are identical to the hand-thrown Frag and Krak Grenade entries above — same warhead, delivered by a launcher tube instead of an arm, which is the standard GURPS approach (a launched grenade uses the grenade's own damage, not a new figure). Acc/range/RoF/shots are new here, since a thrown weapon doesn't carry those stats, and are built as a simple single-shot break-action or revolver launcher: modest accuracy, a much longer practical reach than a throwing arm, and slow reloading between shots.",
